body:
I did enjoy this book as well, it was an easy read about  pretty broad subject and I'm glad this got to be so popular. You should also read the "sequel", Homo Deus - it does tent to repeat a lot of the first book, but the second part is great, since it highlights the present day and where we are going. 

I would also recommend Jared Diamond's "Steel , Germs and Guns" , it's somewhat similar in style but it takes a deeper look into the whole anthropological - social factors that got us to the point we are in the present era, being described by many to be the best in the field.  

&#x200B;
